The lane runs `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` of the whole solution (the template lane's seat measured the build under 3 minutes and the whole-solution test 7 to 9 minutes; the drafter's scratch build took 17 seconds). The project's rule applies to the dotnet jobs: take a slot by atomic `mkdir '<project>/.tools/.heavy-lock-1'` (else `-2`; neither free: poll every 60 s), write `holder.txt` (pane name, label, `date`), run the dotnet jobs of steps 3(b) and 5(e), release by MOVING the holder file to `.tools/b1693/logs/` and `rmdir` your own dir. **Load gate: `LC_ALL=C uptime` load1 under 24 on TWO reads 120 s apart (not independent: say so)** (the product owner's 2026-11-11 ruling for this 18-CPU machine). A holder older than 30 minutes with no live pane is REPORTED, never removed. A wait is not a finding; waited 30 minutes: say so; at the hard stop `BLOCKED: heavy lock waiting at load <n>`.

